# MjengoOS — STAGING environment template (issue #208).
# Copy to `.env.staging` (gitignored — never commit real secrets) and run
# compose with BOTH flags:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.staging -f docker-compose.staging.yml up -d --build
# This file feeds docker-compose.staging.yml ONLY, in two places at once:
# compose's variable interpolation (the fail-closed NEXTAUTH_SECRET check)
# and the app service's env_file. --env-file makes interpolation read THIS
# file instead of the project dir's `.env` — without it, a prod `.env` in
# the same clone would silently feed staging prod's secrets.

# ── REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Auth session secret — REQUIRED, and a NEW one, never prod's (a shared
# secret would let a session minted on one box count on the other).
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32   (or: openssl rand -base64 32)
# The placeholder below is deliberately TOO SHORT so an unedited copy of
# this template fails closed (compose aborts; the app's production boot
# guard would refuse it anyway — staging runs NODE_ENV=production).
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=change-me

# ── Strongly recommended ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The base URL your team browses staging at. The default is correct when
# verifying on the staging host itself; change it to the host/LAN address
# the team actually uses (e.g. http://staging-box:3100). Behind a proxy?
# Leave it unset and keep AUTH_TRUST_HOST=1 (the §7.1 lesson).
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3100

# Trust forwarded host/proto headers (needed if a proxy ever fronts
# staging; harmless for direct access — same value the dev .env ships).
AUTH_TRUST_HOST=1

# Background-job drain token (the jobs-tick sidecar): the SAME value
# reaches the app (env_file) and the sidecar (compose interpolation) from
# THIS file. Generate a NEW one — never prod's: openssl rand -hex 32.
# UNSET (default) = the bearer path is disabled and every tick 401s (the
# sidecar's startup banner explains the fix) — fine for a staging box that
# only needs the app + website.
# JOBS_RUN_TOKEN=

# ── Everything else ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every variable documented in .env.example / DEPLOYMENT.md §3 applies
# unchanged; anything set here reaches the staging app via env_file.
# Deliberately NOT set here:
#   DATABASE_URL    — compose pins it to the staging volume
#                     (file:/app/db/custom.db on staging-app-db);
#   USSD_WEBHOOK_SECRET / WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_SECRET — staging runs
#     NODE_ENV=production, so unset secrets mean the field-line webhooks
#     fail closed (503) — the correct staging posture too;
#   the Daraja block — sandbox callbacks cannot reach a NAT'd staging box;
#     the simulated payment provider (the default) is what staging should
#     run;
#   S3_*            — staging exercises the default local-disk upload path.
